{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" datamodel=\"xpath\" initial=\"s\">\n  <datamodel><data id=\"list\"><a/><a/></data></datamodel>\n  <state id=\"s\">\n    <onentry>\n      <foreach array=\"$list/a\" item=\"$it\" index=\"$i\">\n        <log expr=\"$it\"/>\n        <log expr=\"$i\"/>\n      </foreach>\n    </onentry>\n    <transition event=\"go\" target=\"f\"/>\n  </state>\n  <final id=\"f\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml039-xpath-foreach-dollar-item.scx"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":0,"notes":0,"total":2,"warnings":2},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml039-xpath-foreach-dollar-item.scx"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":1,"byteOffset":217,"endColumn":39,"endLine":5,"startColumn":38,"startLine":5},"insertedContent":{"text":""}}]}],"description":{"text":"remove the `$`"},"properties":{"applicability":"machine-applicable"}}],"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml039-xpath-foreach-dollar-item.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":39,"endLine":5,"startColumn":38,"startLine":5}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`<foreach item>` names the variable `it`, which is written without `$`\n\n**Note:** `<foreach>` binds each item (and its position) to the variable named by `item`, declaring it when needed, and expressions then read it as `$it`; `item=\"$it\"` is instead a location that assigns to an existing variable `$it`, and none is declared, so the loop raises `error.execution`\n\n**Help:** write the variable name without `$`: `item=\"it\"`\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §4.6 <foreach>\n\n**Spec:** SCXML CR 2014 §C.3.10 <foreach>","text":"`<foreach item>` names the variable `it`, which is written without `$`"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":218,"start":217},"category":"lint"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"in this `item`"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml039-xpath-foreach-dollar-item.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":41,"endLine":5,"startColumn":38,"startLine":5}}}],"ruleId":"SCXML039"},{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml039-xpath-foreach-dollar-item.scx"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":1,"byteOffset":229,"endColumn":51,"endLine":5,"startColumn":50,"startLine":5},"insertedContent":{"text":""}}]}],"description":{"text":"remove the `$`"},"properties":{"applicability":"machine-applicable"}}],"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml039-xpath-foreach-dollar-item.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":51,"endLine":5,"startColumn":50,"startLine":5}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`<foreach index>` names the variable `i`, which is written without `$`\n\n**Note:** `<foreach>` binds each item (and its position) to the variable named by `index`, declaring it when needed, and expressions then read it as `$i`; `index=\"$i\"` is instead a location that assigns to an existing variable `$i`, and none is declared, so the loop raises `error.execution`\n\n**Help:** write the variable name without `$`: `index=\"i\"`\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §4.6 <foreach>\n\n**Spec:** SCXML CR 2014 §C.3.10 <foreach>","text":"`<foreach index>` names the variable `i`, which is written without `$`"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":230,"start":229},"category":"lint"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"in this `index`"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml039-xpath-foreach-dollar-item.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":52,"endLine":5,"startColumn":50,"startLine":5}}}],"ruleId":"SCXML039"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"`location`, `idlocation`, `namelist` items, and `<foreach item/index>` must name an assignable place; SCXML 1.0 defines the run-time outcome of one that does not, so the document compiles: §5.9.2 \"If a location expression cannot be evaluated to yield a valid location, the SCXML processor MUST place the error 'error.execution' in the internal event queue\", and §4.6 \"if 'item' does not specify a legal variable name, the SCXML processor MUST terminate execution of the <foreach> element and the block that contains it, and place the error error.execution on the internal event queue\". In ECMAScript an assignable place is a variable or a property access such as `data.field` or `data[0]`; in XPath it is an expression that selects existing nodes, such as `$data` or `$data/field` (`a.b` is one variable name containing a dot, and `a[0]` is a predicate)"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: ECMAScript: use a variable name or a member expression such as `data.field`; XPath: use a `$`-rooted path to a declared variable such as `$data/field`.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §5.9.2 Location Expressions\n\nRun `scx --explain SCXML039` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#LocationExpressions","id":"SCXML039","name":"SCXML039","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"a location is not assignable in the selected data model"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}